lementation-date\">June 18, 1999<br/>Beta 5.0</span></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\">See also: Objects<span class=\"explained\">Help</span></nav>\n</aside>\n<div id=\"w-twbox-intro\">\n<div id=\"w-object-profile\">\n<div id=\"w-twbox-image\"><img alt=\"latest?cb=20070205185214&amp;path-prefix=en&amp;format=original\" class=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Scarf_457976.gif\"/></div>\n<div id=\"w-twbox-look\"><div class=\"item-look tibiatext tibiagreen\">You see a scarf <span class=\"p-attributes\">(Arm:1)</span>.<div class=\"p-weight\">It weighs 2.00 oz.</div><br/></div></div>\n<div class=\"\" id=\"w-twbox-sounds\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:left;\"></div>\n<div id=\"w-object-notes\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Notes\">Notes</span></h3>\n<p>Scarfs don't have any special effects. They increase body armor with 1 armor point. A player who can't afford a <a href=\"#/wiki/Platinum%20Amulet\">Platinum Amulet</a> could wear a scarf. This item can be bought in <a href=\"#/wiki/Edron\">Edron</a> by premium players and sold for much higher prices to a Free Account (who is unable to travel to <a href=\"#/wiki/Edron\">Edron</a> to buy his own). It is also possible to get them at the <a href=\"#/wiki/Daily%20Respawns\">daily spawn</a> inside a corpse that you can reach by entering the <a href=\"#/wiki/Desert%20Dungeon\">Desert Dungeon</a> and going all the way down and then in the room with the <a href=\"#/wiki/Spider\">Spiders</a> all the way up.\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:left;\"></div>\n<div id=\"w-item-droppedby\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Dropped_By\">Dropped By</span></h3>\n<div class=\"item-droppedby-wrapper\">\n<ul><li><a href=\"#/wiki/Cult%20Believer\">Cult Believer</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#/wiki/Cult%20Enforcer\">Cult Enforcer</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#/wiki/Cult%20Scholar\">Cult Scholar</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"#/wiki/Grynch%20Clan%20Goblin\